  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the hyperbolic cylinder $(x+5)^{2}-{y}^{2}=1?$",
  "worked_solution": "The full expression describing all points on our hyperbolic cylinder is\n\n$$\n(x+5)^{2}-{y}^{2}=1,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{\u00a0}(x+5)^{2}-{y}^{2}=1}.\n$$\n\nThis is a hyperbola centered at $(-5,0).$",
